{
  "country": "SE",
  "name": { "en": "Sweden", "sk": "Švédsko", "sv": "Sverige" },
  "source": "Lag (1989:253) om allmänna helgdagar (National Day a holiday from 2005, Whit Monday until 2004); Midsummer Eve, Christmas Eve and New Year's Eve are equated with Sundays by Semesterlag (1977:480) 3 a § and Arbetstidslag (1982:673). Verified 2026-10-04.",
  "notes": "Easter Sunday and Whit Sunday (always Sundays) and Midsummer Day and All Saints' Day (always Saturdays) are left out. Midsummer Eve, Christmas Eve and New Year's Eve are not 'röda dagar' but are days off for almost everyone.",
